<title>BELGIUM: EU to vote on cereals, oilseed non-food changes.</title>
<headline>EU to vote on cereals, oilseed non-food changes.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee will on Thursday vote on proposals to change rules for aid payments to farmers growing cereals and oilseeds on set-aside land for industrial uses, EU sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;The aim is to ensure that the aid is being properly used,&quot; said one source.</p>
<p>The changes require member states to set representative cereals and oilseed yields each year. Farmers would be penalised if they failed to achieve the yields.</p>
<p>The representative yields could be set for each farm, district, region or country.</p>
<p>High erucic acid oilseed varieties would be excluded from the new rules.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
